    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>DogSitting à Nice is a home-boarding service based in the Fabron neighbourhood of Nice. Its distinctive point, as advertised by the provider: since the dog sitter works from home, your dog would be the only animal hosted during its stay, rather than being kept alongside several other boarders.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The service advertises a fairly wide coverage area for home boarding: Nice, Cannes, Monaco, Cagnes-sur-Mer and Antibes. Full boarding (accommodation, meals, outings) would be offered at around €18 per day according to the information found online, and daily walks are included in the package. <strong>These prices and availability should be reconfirmed directly</strong> with the provider, as the information available online for this service is limited (few reviews published so far). As with any boarding at a private individual's home, plan a meeting with your dog before booking a stay.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the "single dog" format can be reassuring for a timid animal or one not very sociable with other dogs — but check this point directly with the dog sitter before booking, as offerings in this field change fast.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Fabron is a residential neighbourhood in western Nice, between the sea and the hills, close to the Promenade des Anglais and a few minutes from Saint-Laurent-du-Var or Cagnes-sur-Mer.</p>
